{
  "id": "Compound::DB00307 - Disease::DOID:2531",
  "verbalization": "Bexarotene, a retinoid, is implicated in the treatment of hematologic cancer through multiple interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Bexarotene, as part of the retinoid family, is linked to the treatment of hematologic cancer via its inclusion in the broader retinoid category, which includes Alitretinoin. This implies a potential role in modulating cellular processes associated with hematologic malignancies. Additionally, Bexarotene's ability to cause hypolipidaemia and its association with doxorubicin, an antineoplastic agent, further supports its involvement in the treatment of hematologic cancer. The presence of Bexarotene in the targeted therapy agent category, alongside its role in causing lichenoid keratosis, adds to the complexity of its biological interactions. These findings collectively suggest that Bexarotene may exert its therapeutic effects through mechanisms that involve both retinoid signaling and antineoplastic action, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
